 are a kind of relief that  Justice in a way is done even though the  four accused were not here in the  courtroom and may probably never go to  jail we don't know this however as we  are sentenced to life arrest warrants  were immediately handed down and so they  can follow the foreseeable future not  leave Russia because they would be  arrested wherever in the world they  turned up before the time being they are  safe there and that of course is an  aspect that some of the relatives here  say still hurts them because they would  of course want to see them go to jail  however justice has been done in a way  maybe in a rather abstract manner but  this Dutch court has really tried to  lead the most the fairest trial possible  under the circumstance answers to sort  of weigh the evidence very carefully to  very carefully think about the chain of  command in 2014 in eastern Ukraine and  the personal responsibility of the  accused and this is the result that we  just heard  now what more can you say about the  verdicts themselves  and the verdict of course was based on a  chain of evidence that was rather  difficult for the Dutch the Dutch Court  to assess because some of it was open  source that was like telephone calls  between the eqs that have been monitored  at the time there were satellite images  how the book missile that was  responsible for the uh or that was of  you know functioning as the missile that  shot down uh the the flight image 17  where it was moved from where it was  moved to and who had the command over  those Rebel militants there who were  active in the area at the time and so  three of the defendants have been now  found guilty that they were in fact the  commanders who did uh who did have  responsibility for what happened in the  area had responsibility for moving this  missile of course with the intent to  shoot down military planes Ukrainian  planes but they by accident they shot  down this passenger plane with its 298  people on board all of them died as we  know and still they are responsible for  what happened at that point  Barbara you've been following this story  closely for for more than eight years  since that fateful crash now uh since  they will likely never go the three uh  that were centers will likely never go  to prison what kind of closure would  will this bring uh to the families  it is for some a part it's some bit of  closure some say they are satisfied with  it because they have seen that a a  criminal court has very carefully  considered the evidence in this case and  said yes they are guilty they're  responsible so justice has been done the  verdict has been spoken so if that  satisfies you in your mind and soul then  this is a step maybe for healing the  wounds that were really inflicted eight  years ago for others however it means  still that they say these people will  never go to jail we don't really expect  it and also the most important Point  nobody no court in the world and nothing  can ever bring their relatives that they  lost in their many tragic cases  um of people who lost their whole  families a wife and three children for  instance some of them on that flight and  whose life more or less has been  destroyed and this court here even  though it tried to be as objective as  Fair and do the best legal job it could  can never bring them back  Barbara basil they're reporting from  Amsterdam thank you very much Barbara
 

